2890 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Parameter 2\072 ICP Specificity\n\nThe question being answered\072 \042Is this for me\077\042\n\nB2B buyers do an instant self\055qualification check\056 If the page doesn\047t signal who it\047s for within the first scroll\054 the right person leaves\056 They simply assume it\047s not for them\056\n\nWhat to look for\072\n\nIs there an explicit signal of who this is for\077 \050Persona\054 company type\054 industry\054 team size\054 or use case context\051\nIs the ICP defined by behaviour\057context or just firmographics\077 \050\042For RevOps teams running multi\055channel outbound\042 is better than \042For B2B companies\042\051\nDoes the ICP signal appear in the hero\054 or is it buried in a \042who it\047s for\042 section three scrolls down\077\n\nScoring guide\072\n\n5\072 ICP is clear in the hero \055 persona\054 context\054 or use case is explicit\n4\072 ICP is identifiable within the first scroll\054 but relies on inference\n3\072 ICP is named somewhere on the page but the hero is generic\n2\072 ICP is implied only through the features listed\054 not stated\n1\072 Page could be for anyone with no qualification signals\n\nFailure pattern\072 \n\nMostly horizontal products that are afraid to exclude anyone\054 so they speak to everyone and resonate with nobody\056 The fix isn\047t niching down the overall product but to choose which use case to lead with on the homepage\056\n\nFill your Score \072)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 2891 0 R
     /Pg 712 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

