2893 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Parameter 3\072 Problem Framing\n\nThe question being answered\072 \042Do they understand what I\047m dealing with\077\042\n\nThis is the empathy parameter\056 Buyers don\047t buy products but exits from their existing problems\056 If the homepage doesn\047t demonstrate that the company understands the problem from the buyer\047s perspective\054 everything else \050features\054 benefits\054 proof\051 just doesn\031t land\056\n\nWhat to look for\072\n\nIs the problem stated from the buyer\047s point of view\054 or the seller\047s\077\nDoes the problem framing describe a specific situation or pain\054 or is it generic \050\042teams struggle with collaboration\042\051\077\nIs the \042current way\042 i\056e\056 how buyers solve this problem today without the product\054 acknowledged\077\nDoes the page explain why the current way is inadequate\077\n\nScoring guide\072\n\n5\072 Specific\054 buyer\055language problem with the current\055way failure clearly named\n4\072 Problem is present and directionally right\054 but framed in seller language\n3\072 Problem is implied through feature descriptions\054 not stated directly\n2\072 Problem framing is so generic it applies to 50 other categories\n1\072 No problem framing\056 Jumps straight to features or aspirational outcomes\n\nFailure pattern\072 \n\n\042Your team deserves better\042 kinda copy that names no specific problem\056 Or leading with the problem from a market\055level \050\042\044X billion is wasted annually\042\051 rather than the individual buyer\047s day\055to\055day struggle and reality\056\n\nFill your Score \072)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 2894 0 R
     /Pg 948 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

