2896 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Parameter 4\072 Value Proposition Clarity\n\nThe question being answered\072 \042What specifically do I get and why should I want it\077\042\n\nThis is distinct from category and problem framing\056 The value proposition is the bridge between the problem you\047ve named\054 here\047s what the product actually does about it and what that means for the buyer\047s world\056\n\nWhat to look for\072\n\nIs there a clear articulation of what the product does \050capability\051 and not just what outcomes it promises\077\nDoes the value proposition connect a specific capability to a specific outcome in one logical step\077\nIs the promised outcome something the ICP actually cares about\054 or a second\055order benefit they\047ll have to work backwards from\077\nDoes the homepage \042sell the drill\042 \050what the product is and does\051 before it sells the \042quarter\055inch hole\042 \050the outcome\051\077 Benefits without capabilities are unconvincing\056\n\nScoring guide\072\n\n5\072 Capability \053 first\055order outcome clearly stated and buyer can immediately visualise the result\n4\072 Good outcome framing but the capability that produces it is vague\n3\072 Either only features \050no outcome\051 or only outcomes \050no capability\051\n2\072 Value proposition is a generic claim \050\042save time\054 reduce costs\042\051 with no specificity\n1\072 No coherent value proposition with page being a list of features or a mission statement\n\nFailure pattern\072 \n\n\042Increase revenue by X\045\042 claims with no explanation of how\056 Or capability\055only pages \050feature dumps\051 with no articulation of what changes in the buyer\047s day\056\n\nFill your Score \072)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 2897 0 R
     /Pg 1190 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

