2899 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Parameter 5\072 Differentiation\n\nThe question being answered\072 \042Why this over everything else I could use\077\042\n\nThis is the most commonly skipped parameter at Series A companies\056 They assume the visitor knows the competitive landscape\054 or they\047re afraid of naming alternatives\056 The result\072 messaging sounds identical to three other direct competitors\056\n\nWhat to look for\072\n\nDoes the page articulate what makes this product different from alternatives and not just what it does\077\nAre the stated differentiators genuine and specific \050a feature\054 a methodology\054 a data advantage\051\054 or generic claims \050\042easy to use\042\054 \042built for enterprise\042\051\077\nDoes the page acknowledge what the competitor set is \050named tools\054 spreadsheets\054 manual processes\051\077\nIs differentiation present in the hero\054 or buried in a comparison table two\055thirds down\077\n\nScoring guide\072\n\n5\072 Specific\054 credible differentiator named and substantiated in the hero or first scroll\n4\072 Differentiator is present but stated as a claim without proof\n3\072 Differentiator is implied by a comparison table lower on the page\n2\072 \042Easy to use \057 powerful \057 flexible\042 type language which doesn\031t differentiate from anything in a meaningful way\n1\072 No differentiation signal at all\056 Page could be lifted and placed on a competitor\047s site and yet nothing changes\056\n\nFailure pattern\072 \n\nPages that list features instead of differentiators\056 Being feature\055complete is not a differentiator\054 it\047s at times baseline expectation\056 The differentiator is the specific thing a competitor can\047t or won\047t do\056\n\nFill your Score \072)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 2900 0 R
     /Pg 1414 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

