2902 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Parameter 6\072 Hero Section Coherence\n\nThe question being answered\072 \042Does the hero\055page elements work as a system\077\042\n\nThe hero section \050headline\054 sub\055headline\054 visual\054 and primary CTA\051 is the single highest\055leverage piece of real estate on a homepage\056 These four elements need to work together\054 not independently\056 Most hero sections have each of these element optimised separately and the whole is incoherent\056\n\nWhat to look for\072\n\nHeadline\072 Does it carry a clear message\054 or is it a tagline\057slogan that sacrifices clarity for cleverness\077\nSub\055headline\072 Does it complete\054 extend\054 or add specificity to the headline or simply repeat it in different or more words\077\nVisual\072 Is it a product screenshot\057demo that adds information or a stock illustration\057abstract graphic that adds nothing\077\nCTA\072 Does the CTA text reflect where the visitor is in their journey \050early\055stage research vs\056 ready to buy\051\054 or is it a generic \042Get Started\042\077\nDoes the above\055the\055fold section answer at least \042what is it\042 and \042is it for me\042 without scrolling\077\n\nScoring guide\072\n\n5\072 All four elements work as a system\056 Above\055the\055fold answers what \053 who it\031s for without scrolling\n4\072 Three of four elements strong\073 minor gap in coherence\n3\072 Hero contains the right elements but they feel assembled independently\n2\072 Hero leads with brand\057aspiration language that delays value communication\n1\072 Hero is a full screen image\054 video background\054 or slogan with no informational content\n\nFailure pattern\072 \n\n\042Headline is the vision\054 sub\055headline is the tagline\054 visual is a gradient with floating UI elements\054 CTA says \047Get Started\047\056\042 \n\nFill your Score \072)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 2903 0 R
     /Pg 1654 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

