2905 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Parameter 7\072 Messaging Hierarchy \046 Page Flow\n\nThe question being answered\072 \042Does the page make logical sense while scrolling and answer my next probable question\042\n\nIndividual sections can be strong while the overall page is incoherent\056 Messaging hierarchy is about whether the page is structured as a persuasion sequence or just a collection of sections that someone thought were important\056\n\nWhat to look for\072\n\nDoes the page follow a logical sequence\072 problem acknowledgment \222 capability\057product \222 proof \222 differentiation \222 conversion\077\nAre there abrupt topic shifts or \034Hey\054 look how great we are\035 sections that break the visitor\047s thinking\077\nDoes the page tell you what to pay attention to at each stage or do all sections feel equal in weight\077\nIs the page length appropriate\077 Too short loses persuasive power\073 too long loses attention\056\n\nScoring guide\072\n\n5\072 Clear persuasion sequence\054 each section builds on the last with appropriate lengths\n4\072 Right sections present but sequencing is slightly off \050e\056g\056\054 proof before problem\051\n3\072 Sections feel modular and interchangeable with no narrative thread\n2\072 Page jumps between topics without connection and sections feel independently designed\n1\072 No discernible structure\056 Page is either a feature dump or an about\055us page\n\nFailure pattern\072 \n\nSocial proof \050customer logos\051 appearing before the problem or value proposition has been established\056 Logos before a visitor knows what you do create no impact since the visitor haven\047t decided if they care yet or not\056\n\nFill your Score \072)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 2906 0 R
     /Pg 1908 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

