2908 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Parameter 8\072 Social Proof Quality\n\nThe question being answered\072 \042Can I trust that this works for someone like me\077\042\n\nSocial proof at Series A is almost always present but rarely doing real work\056 The question is not \042do they have testimonials\042 but \042are the testimonials doing the job of reducing the specific doubts a buyer has at this stage\077\042\n\nWhat to look for\072\n\nAre testimonials specific \050named person\054 company\054 outcome\051 or generic claims\077\nDo testimonials address the specific objections a Series A buyer has \050implementation risk\054 ROI\054 switching cost\051\077\nAre customer logos representative of the ICP or a mix of logos thrown together for brand recognition\077\nIs there third\055party validation \050G2 ratings\054 analyst mentions\054 press\051 or only first\055party claims\077\nAre the numbers cited \050customers\054 ARR\054 outcomes\051 specific and credible or round\054 vague\054 and unprovable\077\n\nScoring guide\072\n\n5\072 Specific testimonials with named outcomes\054 logos match ICP\054 third\055party validation present\n4\072 Testimonials are specific but don\047t address key objections\073 logos are right audience\n3\072 Testimonials are generic but present\073 logos are recognisable but not ICP matched\n2\072 Only logos\054 no testimonials\073 or testimonials with no names\057outcomes\n1\072 No social proof\054 or social proof that raises more questions than it answers\n\nFailure pattern\072 \n\nFive enterprise logos from the pilot cohort that don\047t represent the ICP\054 paired with three testimonials that say \042intuitive interface\042 and \042great customer support\056\042\n\nFill your Score \072)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 2909 0 R
     /Pg 2142 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

