2911 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Parameter 9\072 Competitive Positioning Awareness\n\nThe question being answered\072 \042Does the company know who they\047re competing with and does the page reflect that\077\042\n\nThis is a PMM\055specific parameter that auditors often miss\056 A homepage can have clear messaging\054 good proof\054 and strong CTAs and still lose deals because it doesn\047t address the competitive context the buyer is already in\056 By the time a Series A buyer visits your homepage\054 they\047ve usually already visited two or three competitors\056\n\nWhat to look for\072\n\nDoes the page acknowledge what alternatives exist \050competitors\057 incumbent tools\057 manual processes\051\077\nIf a comparison page or \042vs\042 section exists\054 is it genuinely differentiating or just a green\055checkmarks table\077\nDoes the page speak to a buyer who is already evaluating alternatives and not just a first\055time category discoverer\077\n\nScoring guide\072\n\n5\072 Competitive context explicitly addressed\054 differentiation from alternatives is substantiated\n4\072 Competitive awareness implied through positioning choices\073 comparison page exists and is useful\n3\072 Comparison section present but generic and competitive context not visible in hero\n2\072 Page assumes no competition and doesn\047t acknowledge alternatives exist\n1\072 Page actively avoids competitive context\073 positioning could apply to any player in the category\n\nFailure pattern\072 \n\nPages that list capabilities without ever acknowledging what the buyer is currently using\056 \042We do X\042 without \042better than Y\042 is an incomplete message for a buyer who\047s already comparing\056\n\nFill your Score \072)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 2912 0 R
     /Pg 2394 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

